# 0084-attach-update-dlc-mods-cheats-and-cloud-covers.patch -- before the first build: its mods and cheats, its update and DLC (several files at once, one removed again); and the covers of the
# NAS / Files games before their download (why the owner saw none, and the fix: .nsz and .nup too, one NAS session, a cache, one log line per game).
# Applies after 0083. Goes with two changes outside app/patches (the repository's own files): crates/ibuilder-ffi ibuilder_nup_icon_read (+ include/ibuilder.h, tests/nup_icon.rs) and
# app/gameapp_shim_rust.c gameapp_nup_icon_read. UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, the Rust tested, the pure C# in the host harness (below).
#
# 1. MODS AND CHEATS BEFORE THE FIRST BUILD: the not-built game's "…" sheet (0082) and its long-press menu gain "Mods and cheats…", the existing Mods page (GameAppModsUi.cs: Atmosphere romfs /
#    exefs / cheats from a .zip or a folder, a switch per mod, per .pchtxt block and per cheat). The page gains "A cheat file (.txt)…" (Import-mode picker): an Atmosphere cheat file
#    named after the build id (atmosphere/contents/<tid>/cheats/<build id>.txt) becomes the mod "Cheats <8 digits>" through GameMods.Import (CheatImport, GameMods.ImportCheatFile), its
#    cheats switched one by one. The mods store is per title id (Documents/games/<tid>/mods), so what is chosen before the build is applied by that first build: the chain plans the
#    exefs patches in every rewrite (crates/ibuilder-pipeline rewrite.rs mods_plan, checked), the RomFS files and cheats at each boot. Built games keep their Mods page in the sheet.
# 2. UPDATE AND DLC IN THE BUILD: "Add an update or DLC…" in the not-built sheet, in a local game's long-press menu and in the built sheet's "Update and DLC" row: Pick files… (the
#    Import-mode picker, AllowsMultipleSelection; the Open-mode pickers deliver nothing on the owner's iOS 27.2.1), Find them in a folder… (0062's scan, now a list with a tick per file:
#    ChecklistSheet), From the cloud (N)… (the NAS / Files candidates, a tick each, downloaded by 0079's Download). Each picked file is classified by title id (ContentAttach.Classify:
#    this game's update or DLC, else refused with a short reason: another game, the base game, not a game file, a .nup, no title id); the valid ones are moved in by CopyIn (the import
#    record: 0068 / 0073 can free them later), the others' copies deleted; one answer ("Attached: … Not attached: … (why)"). The Build row says what the build will merge ("23.9 GB · Not
#    built · update v131072 · 1 DLC", ContentAttach.Summary, the chain's own UpdateFor / DlcFor); "Remove <update / DLC>…" in the not-built sheet removes one (0062's RemoveFiles question).
#    The chain merges them as before: the update is the extractor's update argument (BeginRunWithArguments UpdateFor), each DLC's RomFS is games/<id>/aoc (ExtractDlc). A .nup carries its
#    update inside the package: no "Add an update or DLC" for it (refused with that reason if picked).
# 3. COVERS BEFORE THE DOWNLOAD. Why the owner saw none (from the code, 0079's FetchCloudIcons): (a) every outcome went to stderr only (Console.Error), never to the app's log, so a failure
#    or a "no icon" was invisible; (b) nothing at all without prod.keys, silently; (c) a .nup on the NAS was never tried (gameapp_nup_icon needs a local path); (d) a failed read (one SSH
#    connection per cover, a timeout) was retried only at the next launch, silently; (e) a compressed control NCA (.ncz of an .nsz) or a personalised ticket gave "no icon" with no word. NOW
#    (FetchCloudCovers, GameAppAttachUi.cs; CloudCovers, GameAppAttach.cs): .nsp .xci .nsz read with prod.keys (the control NCA; an .ncz one is said), a .nup read over SFTP through the new
#    ibuilder_nup_icon_read (its head: superblock, table of contents, meta block, NPDMs; no keys), ONE NAS session for the whole pass (Nas.WithSession), a Files folder opened once, a cache
#    per remote file (Documents/gameapp.cloudcovers.tsv: source, remote path, size, outcome; a file of another size is read again; a cached icon whose file is gone is read again; the cloud
#    listing keeps no modification time, so size stands in for it), off the main thread after the listing, never while a build runs, one line per game in the log ("cover: X (On the NAS):
#    read before the download" / "none: <why>" / "needs prod.keys" / "read failed: <why> (tried again at the next launch)"). Greyed with the cloud badge as before, the real cover under it.
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-21, M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: every patch applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree. Compile (-t:Compile):
#   0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as before 0080 (the two Import-mode pickers' obsolete-API warnings silenced on their lines, as 0067 did). Rust: cargo test -p
#   ibuilder-ffi all pass (nup_icon 6 of 6, 2 new: the callback gives the same icon and title as the file, a failing / short / foreign reader is an error, bad arguments refused), cargo
#   clippy -p ibuilder-ffi --all-targets -D warnings clean, cargo fmt clean; the shim compiles (xcrun clang -fsyntax-only -Wall, arm64-apple-ios26.0, no warning). Host harness (harness84:
#   PAD81;P82;P83;P84, GameAppAttach.cs and GameAppMods.cs added): 203 of 203 checks (25 new, among them the REAL GameMods.ImportCheatFile on a scratch Documents); 10 of 10 mutations killed.
# NOT VERIFIED: no device: the pickers, the lists, a .nup cover over a real SFTP server, the cache across launches, the time a pass takes on the owner's NAS.
# NEW UI STRINGS: "Mods and cheats…", "Add an update or DLC…", "Add an update or DLC", "Pick files… (several at once)", "Find them in a folder…", "From the cloud (", "Attach to ",
#   "Downloaded, then merged by the build.", "Attached: ", "Not attached: ", "Nothing was picked.", "Remove ", "A cheat file (.txt)…", "Not a cheat file", the CheatImport.NeedsBuildId text,
#   "it belongs to another game", "it is the base game, not an update or a DLC", "a Switch 2 package: its update is inside it", "Add ", "Matched by title id; copied (or cloned) into iBuilder,
#   then merged by the build."; log lines "cover: ", "attach: ", "needs prod.keys", "read before the download".
